WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:03.860
So we've got some major breaking news on the
show up.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.689
Producer Pat Ford

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:12.169
is sadly no longer producer for the David
Pakman show, but he's not gone.

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:18.300
He is now moving on to a new shiny position
being supervising producer for the David Pakman

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.300
show.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.300
Pat's been here for a couple of years.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.300
He's not leaving.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.300
He got a promotion.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.970
We're going to be ramping up a whole bunch
of new initiatives on the show.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.710
The one sad thing for some people, uh, about
all this is that you're not going to be hearing

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:38.850
from pat and nearly as much on the broadcast
show, which includes podcasts, radio, TV,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.870
and sort of like our normal youtube clips.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.579
But Pat is going to be on the daily bonus
show.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:49.260
So anyone, one who wants to continue to hear
and see pat dailies still can and as his new

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:55.130
initiatives get underway, we're actually going
to be hearing more about that from pat on

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:59.579
the bonus show, including what he's working
on, things coming up on the show and a lot

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:00.579
more.

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:02.220
So it's a sort of bittersweet announcement.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.630
It's basically a result of pat just has a
ton of stuff to do and a lot more now that

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.119
he is going to be supervising the production
of the show.

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:15.630
And uh, this has been, you know, going back
to the producer Louis days, this has been

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.920
a thing within the producer role for a long
time.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.700
You might remember if you've been with us
this long, when Louis started on the show,

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:28.850
his producer years ago, the idea was that
he'd, uh, not be participating in the show

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:34.899
because of how, uh, the studio was set up
and a bunch of different things.

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:39.579
But at the time, because Louis, his role was
much smaller because remember the show was

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:44.040
like once every other week Louis started kind
of chiming in and some people liked it, some

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.540
people didn't like it.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:49.319
And since then it's been very kind of like
off again on again.

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:53.609
We're sometimes we'd hear from Louis sometimes
not depending on what was going on with the

00:01:53.609 --> 00:02:00.560
show that day or week, same with pat, but
there is so much new stuff going on now, um,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.609
that it's just much more time efficient for
pat to be working on other aspects of the

00:02:06.609 --> 00:02:12.480
show while the show is being produced rather
than monitoring the show's production minute

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.480
to minute.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.079
So we're going to be getting a lot more done
and that's the path forward.

00:02:16.079 --> 00:02:20.430
And I'll tell you about some of the exciting
things that are being added effective immediately

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.519
and or rolled out in the next few weeks.

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:30.930
Number one by significant very popular demand,
we are ramping up subtitles captions and transcripts

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:31.930
for the program.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.549
A ton of people who have asked about this,
some people it's because they're hard of hearing

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:41.569
other people just really like being able to
kind of read along with what we're saying.

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:46.659
Others want to be able to read what's on the
show rather than actually watching the clips.

00:02:46.659 --> 00:02:52.469
So we're going to be immediately implementing
youtube captions and subtitles.

00:02:52.469 --> 00:02:57.640
And then over the short to medium term, we
are also going to be generating daily transcripts

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:03.659
of the show, which you can, uh, read, you
can read on your computer, you'll be able

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:06.900
to read on your mobile phone if you prefer
to sort of like read the show rather than

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.099
listen to it when you're commuting or whatever
else.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:14.220
So that is one thing which is one of the most
common requests and it's actually quite a

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.470
bit of work.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:19.500
Um, surprisingly or not for people who know
what goes into that.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.549
And Pat is going to be spearheading that.

00:03:21.549 --> 00:03:24.549
And then also, this is really great news.

00:03:24.549 --> 00:03:30.300
We're going to be expanding our Facebook video
presence to put the entire shows clips on

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.300
Facebook.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.900
And you might be saying, well what are you
talking about David?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.400
I see your stuff on Facebook already.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.950
Here's how it Kinda how that has evolved over
time.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:44.670
Years ago we would take a youtube clip and
we would embed it on Facebook.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:50.890
Um, a couple of years ago, Facebook started
allowing what we would call native video uploads

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:56.120
to Facebook, which means we're no longer embedding
a youtube clip, but we're directly uploading

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.920
the video to Facebook and you see it in Facebook's
video player.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.620
And we did that a little bit with like 30
or 40% of the show.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:10.219
And then nine months ago Facebook launched
video monetization on Facebook.

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:15.780
So that was an immediate incentive to increase
how much of the show we were uploading to

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:20.720
Facebook and we upped it to like two thirds
of the daily show, but it was making like

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:21.720
no money.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:28.070
Even though it was quote monetized, it was
making I think like 30 bucks a month for the

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:32.510
entire month of, you know, most of the last
nine months.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:37.000
But in the last couple of months, Facebook,
video revenue has started to go up and because

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:42.450
we're always looking for alternatives to youtube
monetization, this is potentially a really

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:48.130
good revenue source for us that can keep sort
of the risk of any one platform failing us

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:51.590
lower by spreading out where we are uploading
video.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.410
So starting effective immediately.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:57.480
We're kind of going to be taking the plunge
and we'll be putting all of the daily show

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:04.710
clips on both youtube and Facebook and that's
another project pat is going to be overseeing.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:10.870
We're looking at posting classic viral clips,
which were on youtube, but we're never on

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:15.970
Facebook to the Facebook page to expose some
of the newer audience to them.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.610
People who haven't seen some of the old classic
viral stuff.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:25.130
And then lastly, we're making a technical
upgrade to the show effective today, which

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:29.640
is going to pretty significantly improve both
the video and audio quality of the show on

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.240
everything but the smallest screen.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:36.120
So if you watch the show on your phone, on
your mobile phone, um, you're probably not

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.340
going to notice much of a difference.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:43.550
But if you're watching on computer monitors
like 20 inches or larger or watching on TV

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:48.250
watching, uh, in high definition, you are
immediately going to see a pretty significant

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.070
visual improvement rolled out over the next
couple of days.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:55.440
So exciting stuff, thanks to everybody's support.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.960
More exciting announcements or upcoming sign
up for memberships.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.940
Of course, that's the best way to support
us.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.550
There's lots of ways to support us now.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.030
Youtube memberships and Facebook subscriptions
or all of that stuff.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:11.690
The best two options, our patrion where we
get 95% of your contribution.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:18.740
Um, and then website memberships where we
get about 97% of your contribution, everything

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:23.360
minus a 2.9% payment processing fee.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.220
So those remain the best ways to support the
show.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.890
Uh, more stuff upcoming very soon and an exciting
announcements.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:31.120
I can't wait to tell you about

